   "lines": [
    "Went on to N.Y.",
    "It is ever so",
    "pleasant to get",
    "home again; I",
    "enjoy college to the",
    "full, and yet I",
    "am always only",
    "too delighted to",
    "get home. Truly",
    "these are the golden",
    "years of my life.",
    "I can not ima-",
    "gine a fellow having",
    "a happier time",
    "than I have had",
    "since I have been",
    "in College."
   ],
